      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0029" n="art0029">
        <head>Thelwall Parish Council,</head>
        <p>Thelwall Parish Council,</p>
        <p>The annual meeting of the Thelwall Parish Coun- cil was held in the echoo!room on Monday evening, I Mr Taylor presiding. There were also present Messrs Hatton, Ford, VI arburton, Houghton, Astall Hewitt, Roebuck, and Cook (clerk). The Clerk read a letter he had sent to the Rural District Council re the Waste-lane nuisance, iv.,king by whom the expense of the improvement would have to be Immo. In reply he had received a communication stating that as it was not in the Thelwali district the Thelwall Council would not have to contribute The election of officers was then proceeded witb On the motion of Mr Hatton,seconded by Mr Astall, Mr Taylor was re-elected chairman for the ensuing year. Messrs Houghton and Roebuck were appointed overseers.</p>
      </div>
