      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0082" n="art0082">
        <head>EARLeST3WN WIN THE CHAMPIONSHIP.</head>
        <p>EARLeST3WN WIN THE CHAMPIONSHIP.</p>
        <p>Earlestown Thursday, the winners of the Montgomery Cup played their lost League mitten, on Thursday evening. on their own ground. The championship cf the Leogue de- pended on the match. Half-Holiday started clown hill, and the play was well co-ttested Rhuebotham opened the scoring for the Thursday from a foul after ten ruinutme play, and this livened up the visitors considerably, and they pressed repeatedly Dutton ran capitally down the wing and centred but Walton cleared the danger. Exciting play took place in the home go lin:Louth, but the defence of the Thursday men, was superb. 1141 f-time score ; Barle.tnwn Thursday I goal Birkenhead half-holiday nil On resuming Esrlestown were quickly to the front, and play was keenly contested in the visitors' half. r. Owen centred grandly, but Lloyd cleared. The Thursday attacked strongly, but met with a. stubborn resistance, Rhuebotham shot over, and then Davies had hard lines with a stinging shot. After twenty five minutes' play le Owen scored the second coal for Baries- town Birkenhead then made desperate efforts to score. but were frustrated. Harlestown returned to the bottom goal, and with a fine shot Rhuebotham banged the ball through for the third time. The result was now beyond it us/It, and Earlestown became the champions of the League. Just on time Birkenhead scored from a penalty. Result : Barlestown Thursday 3 goals, Birkenhead Half-Holiday 1 go a/.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <head>RUGBY FOOTBALL. --- LANCASHIRE SENIOR COMPETITION, WIDNES LOSN THE OrIAMPIONSEIIP. HEAVE DEFEAT AT BARROW.</head>
        <p>RUGBY FOOTBALL. --- LANCASHIRE SENIOR COM- PETITION, WIDNES LOSN THE OrIAMPIONSEIIP. HEAVE DEFEAT AT BARROW.</p>
        <p>Widnes played their last Competition- ;Fitch on Thursday Peacock at made a Barrow. fieAspey k froai which started, ißlioawv k ;as t r mreturned.missed the shot for goal. rnart exchanos gained for Widnes a deal of veund. Bamber got the better of a race with Hughes. who luckily held. liVidaes forced the pace. and Widnes touched down. Grand play by Aspey. Rispan, and P tacottk took His bail to the line. Rispan just failed at the drop. Barrow pressed for a few moments, but Proctor made a mull of the ball enabling Tilley art I Peacock to' gain ground. Wilson scored for Barrow Bowker kicker a goal. Widnes rushed to the line, but were soon driven back by Bowker. Both ends were quickly visited, and in one of these, at the Barr w end, Tilley hid a floe chance to rub off 2 poinots ....tit he failed to raise the ball Aspey and Douglas just missed scoring under the DOS'S. Half-time —Barrow, 5 points ; Widnes, nil. Bowker started, and itsoey made a mark: Laney gave to Rlspan, who passed to Peacock awk- Treweeke dribbled finely, and nearly beat Kinsella. Dailey cleared Barrow from a dangerous position. Bowker was awarded a penalty, but the ball went wide at a shot for goal, and Barrow pressed keenly and pinned Widucs on the line, where Banabor scorel. Bowker nails fated at goal Proctor made amends for this, and dropped a goal. Still Barrow pressed and kept Widnes out. Dailey dropped for Widnes. but missed. Bamber scored for Barrow. &amp;lowed by Treweeke, Result i—Barrow 3 goals four tries 18 points), Widnes nil. This result leave Wigan champions of the Competition, as they are two points Rhea a of Widnes.</p>
