        <p>SOUTH WEST LANCASHIRE • COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>There WWI a fair crowd at Widnes on Saturday to witness the match with Leigh in the abov competition. Considerable excitement was manifested for a win to Widnes meant cmi— peting 1,, the final with Warrington for the cop and medals. Play was generally of a scramnling de c iptiou, he passing on both sides being crude in the extreme. The only points of the match were obtaine 1 by Wldnea through T ,layie+ fool- ishly getting tackled behind his own goal line and losing po- ssession of the bald:Webster thus got alissift try.which Tay'or tett rayed. Sev, rat goo .1 in lividu afforte were male '-fors the close but the score rem iirlefi unaltered. Aridles had the best of a poor game but they were lucky to sore in the manner they did. RUNCORN'S NARROW VICTIRY /IT WIG 407.</p>
        <p>Considering tbe fact. thet Wigen had a weakened team in the field at Springfield Park and that they played fourteen men during the greeter portion of the gime it must be admitted they did exceedingly well In preventing Runcorn registering more than a couple of points against them. Within the first quarter Webster, one of the hnese three: quarters, whilst attempting to (clear, we heavily grassed, with the unfortunate outcome that be sustained injuries which necessitate/ his removal to the lecalialirmary„ Webster had up to this point done ednairsble neesleo fo.. his side, but espite his absence the w,geners continued to bane as much nf the encounter as their noponen's, the Intervel being reached with a clean sheet On the resumption, Tolley gained possession, and neatly r Aotel the lea her over the oross-bar. Later on the Wiganers had a rare chance of getting ahead as the result If a vi g trot. melt by the torwarl+.but In the anxiety to take advantage of a etc r opening close to the Runcorn line Herten knocked on and the opportunity was lost, Jolley's effort being sufficient to establish a viotory for the Ch shire exponents.</p>
