      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0090" n="art0090">
        <head>PROPOSED SECOND DIVISION OF THE</head>
        <p>PROPOSED SECOND DIVISION OF THE</p>
        <p>NORTHERN RUGBY LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>The negotiating between the Northern League and the respective Senior Competitions of Lancasnire and Yorkshire came to a bead on Tuesday night at the Rxchange Hotel. archester, where a joint meeting of the Northern League and the Lancashire senior Competition was held, to consider the goestion of the negotiations between the Yorkshire Senior Competition and the Northern League The latest question was fully considered in Yorkshire last week and the Lancashire Senior Competition Committee pointed out that they were 60 weak numerically thst the adoption of the proposal of the Yorkshire Senior Comoetltion and the con- sequent probable transfer of Hull Kingston Rovers and Brig- house Rangers (the latter being the bottom club in the Northern Union League) from the Lancashire Senior Com- petition to the Yorkshire Senior Competition. wool.) cause their position to be untenable, as they would not have suffi- cient clubs to get tovethsr a satisfactory programme After a discussion of a pro'ongei character, the Lancashire Senior Competition adooted thpfollowing resolution : . . . . .</p>
        <p>" That this Coin ',Wee strongly recommend that a S'OOnd Division of the Northern Rugby League be formed, and that promotion to the Northern Union League be through the proposed Second Division &amp;lon, and that the Northern League invite all eligihie clubs to join." Followiag on the abov, an important resolution, R 9 arrived at by the Northera Rugby League, was given out officially as follows :</p>
        <p>_ . "The tiforthein League Committee, after taking into Con- sideration—(l). In view of the statement of the Yorkshire Senior Competition that t bey had no feeling in respect to their third point. that is. rromorion by merit, and that, in fact, they were not anxious for the same ; (2) the numerical position of the Lancashire Senior Competition. In view o/ the proposed arrangements, unanimously decided to assist the Lancashire Senior Competition in the formation of a strong Sanely! Division of the Northern Rugby League, and, further, that a meeting on the rubj.et he held at aa early date with the Yorkshire Senior Competition." LAnCASHIRH SilliOß CO VIPBTITION.</p>
        <p>A meeting of the committee of this ho iv was held at the Hxchange Hotel, Manchester, on rueridiv evening, Ur J Welch (Stockport) in the Chair. A Shepherd (local, was registered as a player with Hull Ring,ston Rover and J Pale I and W White, both of Widnes Rangers. with Widnes. T Percival was struck off the Widnes list, while Hull Kingston Rovers were fined 20s for late start on April 10th, Rochdale Hornets were reported for being 30 m'nu'es late on April 15th. and their explanation tieing satisfAmory was ace.pted. Bebbingtoia, of Stockport, and Greenup of Altrincharn, were suspended up to and Including September 30th, for rough play on April 12th. The neat item WNS the most important nf the meeting, h. it related to the match between the Champions and the Heat of the Hompetition,Tbe following resolution was passed: ''ln the event of, Widnes winning their remaining two matches,</p>
        <p>which wou,d place them on terms of equality with Wigan, a test m.itch will be played at Warrington on Monday. April 28th Kock-off 6.3 p.m. If, on the other hand, Nidnes fail to equal toe Wig n Club's score the latter club will play tee nest of the Competitlon at ffligan on the s .me date and time. Officials : iteferes. Mr F Benton or Mr J B Shaw ; touch judges, lasers 3 Welch and J Hougtaton.</p>
