        <head>Military Changes.</head>
        <p>Military Changes.</p>
        <p>The following changes an I appointments are milled in the " Gazette" :—The Prince of Wales's Volunt are (South Lancashire Regiment): Lieuten- ants to be capt Inas : 110 Herbert, in succession to Major U G p,ndergast, who holds an extra-regi- mental appoinrment ;IYOrville B DAVITeOrI, vice Brevet, Major E T James, seconded. Warrington Ragged School and Mission. The annual services in connection with the above took place ou Sunday. Mr. R A Naylor, FR GS, delivered two addresses at the afternoon and even- ing services, the sub.le Its being " Ye are wine" and " We are Thine," Solos were rendered by the Misses M. Norris, S .7 Birchen. A Ifigginson and M Birch all. ' Special hymns were rendered by the children assis ed by friends and an orchestra under the conductorship of Mr F Owen, Mr A Woodhouse presided at the organ. The congregations were large and the col- lections amounted to £5 68 511. The children did justice to an excellent tea which was provided at the close of the afternoon service.</p>
