      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0101" n="art0101">
        <head>BOWLING.</head>
        <p>BOWLING.</p>
        <p>L&amp;NCASHIRE AND CHESHIRE ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>The adjourned half-pearly meeting of the abeve Association was held at the Clarence Hotel, Manchester, ,on Tuesday evening, Mr P Fielding in the chair. The balance sheet was produced by the Treasurer, Mr R ' Williamson, sb o wing a deficiency of £3B 4e 7d on the accounts ef the past year. The same having been passed, Mr Rateliffe (Allen's Green) proposed that a special match, the teams to be formed front the players ncminated for taking part in the Yorkshire match from each affiliated club in the Association. All parties present whether players or visitors to pay ls. entrance, the pro- ceeds to go towards the deficiency. This recommenda- tion having been carried, it was decided to make the draw for the opening round of the championship com- petition, the ties in which will have te be played of prior to the sth of May next. The drew resulted as follows, the greens ever which the matches will be trundled being afterwards added by the special com- mittee : _ .</p>
        <p>Douglas v Warrington,nt Newton-le-Willows. Leigh Railway v Whitefield, at Old Trafford. Radcliff v Leigh, at Broughton.</p>
        <p>-01-6;aa—&amp;-rn. v IrLam. at Wirhington. Allen'e green v Stretford, at ttollinwool.</p>
        <p>- Wigan v Withington, a (.3roft'a Bank. Heaton v Bronghtoa, at Ashtoa-on-kleraey.</p>
        <p>• Pendleton v denten Chapel, at Radcliffe Conservative Club. _</p>
        <p>Northenden v Hollirtwood at Heaton Chapel. Newton v Tyldasley, at Wigan. Radcliffe Conservatives v Didsbury, at Kersal Moore. Ashton-on Mersey v o.d Trafford, at Urnaston Victoria. Kenai Moor y li!trpurhev, at Radeliffe.</p>
