        <p>The New Warrington Postmaster. Mr L E Tennent, Postmaster ot Barrow-in-Furness, has been appointed Postmaster of Warrington, to succeed Mr J L Viney, who several weeks ago was appointed to the more responsible position of post- master of Bolton. Teetimonial to the Rev L W Thomas.=l lOn Sunday the offertories at St Paul's Church,were given as a testimonial to the Rev L W Thomas, tbe former curate, who has left for altrincharn to join his late Vicar, the Rev EC It Tarbuck. The collec- tions realised £ll 4s 2d.</p>
        <p>Eisteddfod at St. Helens.—Local Successes At toe St Helens Town Hall, on saturday after- noon and evening, an eisteddfod was held,promoted by the St Helens prize choir. The Rev Wynne Davies. conducted, and Mr Wilfrid Jones, R A M,was the adju.dicator. There was a body of 500 competi- tors, and the following were the awards :—Con- tralto solo, Nlis+. Slaggie Smith, Birkenhead ; piano solo, Miss Williams, Runcorn ; chiliren's choirs, Widnes Technical Class ; recitalon, Miss Maggie Williams. Liverpool ; quartette, Mrs Critchley. Miss Mackenzie, Messrs Powell and Gill, Wigan; soprano solo, Miss Watkins, Earlestown ; Church choirs, Wigan Congregational ;tenor sole, prize divided between Mr Williams, Liverpool, and Mr Edwards, of Ashton ; duet. J Williams,gverton, and R G Davies, Liverpool ; male voice quartette, Mr Threl- fill and party, Southport ; challenge solo, in which the competitors sang their favourite solo, Miss Mabel Cheetham, Pemberton. The competitors in the male voice choir competition were Southport Vocal Union, Nutgrove Male Voice, Garswcpd Wigan Harmonic, Warrington Male Voice, and Openshaw. Wigan were adjudicated first, South- port second, Garswood third,and Warrington fourth</p>
